        <body>
            <div xml:id="d659">

                <pb facs="0519" n="511" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg511"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.115 Panay/330</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Navy Department to the Department of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1937-12-20T23:59:59-05:00"
                            notBefore="1937-12-18T21:10:00-05:00">undated</date>.]<lb/>[Received
                        December 20, 1937.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The following information has been received from the Commander-in-Chief Asiatic
                    Fleet under date of 18 December, 1937: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>In the event that the Japanese Government suggests recalling Admiral
                            Hasegawa as one of the amends for the <hi rendition="#italic">Panay</hi>
                            incident and as press reports from Tokyo indicate that possibility the
                            following is submitted to the department:</p>
                        <p>Admiral Hasegawa has been easy to deal with during the past incident and
                            has been very considerate. Because of his duty in Washington as Naval
                            Attaché he is friendly towards the U. S. I believe that he
                            conscientiously did his utmost to prevent an outbreak of hostilities at
                            Shanghai and that he does not favor the current extreme militaristic
                            policy of his Government. Our difficulties will probably be greatly
                            increased if any other officer replaces him.</p>
                    </quote></p>
            </div>
        </body>
